From e029a23b15925a24d272cbd9d6f6a4f09962bb6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:08:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] layer.conf: declare wrynose compatibility

The layer declares walnascar only. This project builds wrynose (Yocto 6.0)
and has validated the layer against it, so add wrynose to the compat list.

Amending conf/layer.conf is the only mechanism that works: bitbake reads
LAYERSERIES_COMPAT_<layer> immediately after parsing each layer.conf and
then delVar()s it (bitbake lib/bb/cookerdata.py, 'Sadly we can't have nice
things'), specifically so it cannot be overridden from local.conf later.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe specific]
Assisted-by: claude-code:claude-opus-5[1m]
---
 conf/layer.conf | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/conf/layer.conf b/conf/layer.conf
index 30ff800..15e3e07 100644
--- a/conf/layer.conf
+++ b/conf/layer.conf
@@ -10,4 +10,4 @@ BBFILE_PATTERN_meta-deepx-m1 = "^${LAYERDIR}/"
 BBFILE_PRIORITY_meta-deepx-m1 = "6"
 
 LAYERDEPENDS_meta-deepx-m1 = "core"
-LAYERSERIES_COMPAT_meta-deepx-m1 = "walnascar"
+LAYERSERIES_COMPAT_meta-deepx-m1 = "walnascar wrynose"
